<title>FRANCE: Mild earthquake jolts central Algeria.</title>
<headline>Mild earthquake jolts central Algeria.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>An earthquake measuring 3.7 on the Richter scale on Wednesday jolted the central Algerian province of M'sila, the Algerian official news agency APS reported.</p>
<p>The tremor, at 0.06 a.m.(2306 GMT), was centred in Hammam Delaa village, 150 km (90 miles) southeast of Algiers, APS said. No damage or casualties were reported.</p>
